---
/**
 * ServicesHero — the services-area page hero
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Eyebrow, H1, supporting paragraph, one primary and one secondary action, and
 * a documentary image in the right-hand column. Used by `/services` and by
 * every `/services/<slug>` detail page — it is the same device, so it is the
 * same component.
 *
 * WHY ALL COPY IS REQUIRED
 *   This component used to read `services-page.js` directly. When the detail
 *   pages needed the same hero the choice was to duplicate the markup or to
 *   pass the copy in, and this follows the `FinalCTA` precedent: while copy had
 *   defaults, a page could render the hero and silently inherit another page's
 *   wording. Nothing here is optional — including the breadcrumb trail — so a
 *   page cannot ship the wrong hero by forgetting to pass something. Supply the
 *   values from a `src/data/*.js` file.
 *
 * UNLIKE THE HOMEPAGE HERO
 *   The homepage H1 is three stanzas with mandated line breaks. This one is a
 *   single sentence that is free to wrap, so nothing here fixes a break — if it
 *   ever needs one, do it with `text-wrap: pretty` in the stylesheet, not with
 *   <br /> in the markup.
 *
 * WHY THE IMAGE IS SECOND IN THE DOM
 *   Mobile order is eyebrow → heading → copy → actions → image, which is the
 *   source order, so no CSS reordering is needed and the reading order stays
 *   correct for keyboard and screen-reader users. Desktop moves the image into
 *   the right-hand column with grid placement only.
 *
 * WHY THE IMAGE IS OPTIONAL
 *   Added for `/insights`, whose §2 ends with "Do not make the hero overly
 *   large" and whose page carries no frame at all — the presentation it was
 *   given is a compact hero and a text-only directory. `imageKey` and
 *   `imageCaption` are therefore optional and the figure is not rendered when
 *   `imageKey` is absent, which collapses the grid to one column via
 *   `sec-hero--solo`.
 *
 * ── WHAT THE NO-IMAGE HERO DOES WITH THE FREED-UP WIDTH ────────────────────
 * It did nothing, and that was wrong. Collapsing to one column left the copy
 * in a 22ch column on the left and roughly half the band empty beside it: on a
 * 1440px viewport the article H1 stopped around x=696 of a 1216px container and
 * the rest of the row was background. Every written `/insights/<slug>` page
 * renders this branch, so "the hero looks half-finished" was the first thing a
 * reader saw on fourteen pages.
 *
 * The fix splits the copy instead of widening it: the eyebrow and the H1 keep
 * the left column, and the standfirst, the optional tagline and the two actions
 * take the right one (`sec-hero__aside`, grid `1.1fr / 0.9fr` from 768px).
 * Nothing is duplicated from the list below and no new device is invented —
 * it is the editorial "headline left, standfirst right" split, made from the
 * elements this hero already carries. The left column stays at its 22ch
 * measure because that measure is the headline's, not a leftover.
 *
 * ⚠ THE TWO BRANCHES CARRY THE SAME FOUR ELEMENTS. That duplication is the
 * price of not shipping a second hero component (rule 12 in MEMORY.md: add an
 * optional prop, do not copy the component) and of keeping every image-bearing
 * page's markup byte-identical. If you change the standfirst, the tagline or
 * the actions, change BOTH branches — the `imageKey &&` one and the
 * `!imageKey &&` one.
 *
 *   This is an ADDITIVE change: every consumer that passes an image passes the
 *   same values and renders the same markup it did before, which is why the
 *   other ten heroes needed no edit. Same rule as `tagline` below — a new
 *   optional capability, never a second component.
 *
 * Styles live in `services-shared.css` (`.sec-hero*`) — see its header for why
 * that file is separate from the overview page's sheet.
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 */
import Breadcrumbs from '../Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Button from '../Button.astro';
import ArrowLink from '../ArrowLink.astro';
import Media from '../Media.astro';

interface Props {
  /** Trail BELOW "Home" — <Breadcrumbs> prepends it. Always end with the
      current page and leave `href` off that last item. */
  breadcrumbs: Array<{ label: string; href?: string }>;
  eyebrow: string;
  /** The page's single H1. */
  title: string;
  description: string;
  /**
   * Optional brand line under the description.
   *
   * Added for `/about`, whose brief (§01) lists a "Secondary line" separate
   * from the hero paragraph and specifies it as the site tagline. It is
   * optional and unrendered by default, so every existing consumer — the five
   * detail pages and `/how-it-works` — emits byte-identical markup and gains
   * no empty element.
   *
   * Only `/about` passes it today, and the value it passes is `site.tagline`,
   * not a typed string, so the hero and the footer's copy of the same line can
   * never disagree.
   */
  tagline?: string;
  primaryCta: { label: string; href: string };
  secondaryCta: { label: string; href: string };
  /**
   * Key from the image manifest in src/data/media.js — unknown keys throw.
   *
   * Optional. No current consumer omits it: `/insights` was the one page that
   * did, and on 2026-10-02 it left this hero entirely for its own background
   * device (`InsightsHero.astro`). The optional prop stays so a page can still
   * ship a text-only hero without a second component; `imageCaption` is
   * required whenever `imageKey` is given and ignored without it.
   */
  imageKey?: string;
  imageCaption?: string;
  /** Unique per page: the <section> is labelled by this id. */
  titleId?: string;
}

const {
  breadcrumbs,
  eyebrow,
  title,
  description,
  tagline,
  primaryCta,
  secondaryCta,
  imageKey,
  imageCaption,
  titleId = 'sec-hero-title',
} = Astro.props;
---

<section class:list={['sec-hero', !imageKey && 'sec-hero--solo']} aria-labelledby={titleId}>
  <div class="container">
    <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} class="sec-hero__breadcrumbs" />

    <div class="sec-hero__grid">
      <div class="sec-hero__text">
        <p class="eyebrow">{eyebrow}</p>

        <h1 class="sec-hero__title" id={titleId}>{title}</h1>

        {
          imageKey && (
            <>
              <p class="sec-hero__lead">{description}</p>

              {tagline && <p class="sec-hero__tagline">{tagline}</p>}

              <div class="sec-hero__actions">
                <Button href={primaryCta.href} label={primaryCta.label} />
                <ArrowLink href={secondaryCta.href} label={secondaryCta.label} />
              </div>
            </>
          )
        }
      </div>

      {/* The no-image branch's right-hand column. Mobile reads it directly
          under the H1, which is the order the copy already had. */}
      {
        !imageKey && (
          <div class="sec-hero__aside">
            <p class="sec-hero__lead">{description}</p>

            {tagline && <p class="sec-hero__tagline">{tagline}</p>}

            <div class="sec-hero__actions">
              <Button href={primaryCta.href} label={primaryCta.label} />
              <ArrowLink href={secondaryCta.href} label={secondaryCta.label} />
            </div>
          </div>
        )
      }

      {
        imageKey && (
          <figure class="sec-hero__figure">
            <Media
              imageKey={imageKey}
              ratio="4x3"
              priority
              sizes="(min-width: 1180px) 520px, (min-width: 768px) 46vw, 100vw"
              class="sec-hero__media"
            />
            <figcaption class="media-caption">{imageCaption}</figcaption>
          </figure>
        )
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
